            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Herodotus</strong><br>\nHerodotus was born around 484 B.C. in Halicarnassus, a Greek city that is now Bodrum, Turkey. Little is known about his early life, but it is believed that he came from a wealthy family. This background gave him the education and leisure time to travel and collect the stories he would later recount in his histories. His upbringing in a culturally diverse city may have also contributed to his curiosity about foreign lands and peoples.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Herodotus's Travels</strong><br>\nHerodotus traveled extensively for the time, reaching Egypt, Persia, Palestine, and possibly even the Black Sea and the Caspian Sea. During his travels, he gathered information from locals, which later provided the basis for his work. His methods were revolutionary because he recorded not just events and dates but also cultural, sociological, and geographical contexts.</p>\n\n<p><strong>\"The Histories\" by Herodotus</strong><br>\nThe Histories is Herodotus's only known work, and it’s considered the first major narrative history written in the ancient world. It covers the Greco-Persian Wars and includes many digressions on the various countries and cultures Herodotus encountered. The work is remarkable for its research, storytelling, and the attempt to understand historical events from multiple perspectives.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
